    "done_when": "A reuse map is written at /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/s25-coord/s25-reuse-map-review-reflex/reuse-map.md with one row for each deliverable in sections s3, s4 and s5 of a-review-is-sized-to-its-risk. s3 composes one repair node per review round, whose write scope is the union of the findings' paths. s4 lets a clean review of 90 or more with no finding promote the reviewed run itself, confirming the gate and running verify-gate at the merged head. s5 has the reflex review only a settled head, withdraw a queued review when the run resumes, carry a review forward over commits that change no runtime source, and light-review only the commits that do. Each row names the existing functions to extend, as file:line read from main HEAD with git show: the review reflex that dispatches reviews and raises review-missing obligations, the review store and select_review_for_head, reckon/crew/promotion.py's review gate and review_tier, the verify-gate replay, and the obligation producer, at least. Each row states what is present and what is missing, and names any second implementation of the same fact a node must reuse. The map proposes a node split with disjoint write paths. It lists the files peer coordinators are editing now (read the live run pointers under ~/.config/reckon/crew/live and git log --since='6 hours ago'), and says which node must wait for which. It also records two facts measured this session. First, the reflex dispatched a second full review of a run whose only later commits were tests and docs, which s5 would carry forward. Second, a stored review's added_failure_count read 0 while the node's own head arm read EXIT=1 with ten FAILED ids; say where that count is derived and why it disagreed. The manifest names the main HEAD sha the map was read at. Nothing in the repository is edited.",
